+# Automatic model selection lifecycle
+
+Product contract: [typed decisions](../../../../../docs/modules/model-decisions.md).
+
+The existing Provider owner selects the optional decision model. AgentRuntime owns automatic
+first-message decision admission, cancellation, durable receipts and usage through its existing
+artifact and Session stores. No new store, permission mode or default policy is introduced.
+
+The sequencing comparison is Craft `332533f3096d12500012fe089c3f155e32af1c44`
+`packages/server-core/src/decisions/decision-point.ts`: a shared deadline, cancellation and
+request/outcome seam. Fleet retains its existing receipt and usage owners rather than copying
+Craft’s separate decision log.
+
+Only an interactive conversation (including the runtime’s undefined task type default) may route
+a first input explicitly marked `allowAutomaticModelSelection: true`. The marker is frozen in the
+existing submission intent; manual same-model picks, missing legacy markers, page assistants and
+all child/workflow/fork task types retain the offered model. Admission, queue/guide, transcript,
+live/cold projection and canonical edit/retry preserve both true and false without guessing.
+
+An automatic consumer supplies a required Host classification callback: policy/question selection
+does not dispatch inference itself. The Host binds the excerpt, writes a durable unknown intent,
+admits one request with the active turn Stop signal and trace, records observed usage, then saves
+the result. Operation identity binds Session and submission input identity (or an exact input and
+offered-selection digest when an input identity is unavailable; this is a conservative optional-routing fence, not proof of distinct manual submissions). A retained unknown or completed
+intent fences another dispatch after interruption/restart. A fenced retry keeps the offered model,
+not a cached previous tier; original submission intent and resolved Session choice are distinct.
+No missing storage path runs inference.
+
+Only an interactive task's automatically initialized Composer choice may set
+`allowAutomaticModelSelection: true`. The existing command/intent owners freeze and retain this
+marker through admission, queue/Guide, messages, events and cold projection. A manual pick of the
+same standard model or its parameters clears it; Project recent choices and unmarked legacy drafts
+remain fixed. Page/child/fork/side task types and execution-scoped turns cannot consume this path.
+
+A first prompt exceeding 6000 characters is incomplete for this consumer and abstains without
+sending a truncated excerpt.
+
+Stop is checked before and after the optional operation and before applying a replacement model.
+The consumer revalidates policy, tiers and target availability after the answer; withdrawal retains
+the offered model. Billed usage remains observable when post-response validation/publication fails.
+A failed usage-ledger write retains the frozen original receipt through the existing
+`runtime/pending_model_usage` SessionEntry seam. Turn settlement and cold resume reconcile the
+same ledger ID, including a committed write whose acknowledgement was lost; inference never replays.
+The main model context/account meter remains owned by the main request, separate from decision cost.
+Provider-keyed active account bindings remain intact. A cross-provider routed intent never copies
+the offered provider's account ID; the existing request-auth owner binds the target. Guide
+availability follows the final executor, not the initially offered model.
+
+Acceptance: isolated real SQLite/artifact restart tests prove one submission, usage and unknown
+fencing, failed usage writes and committed acknowledgement loss; delayed fixture answers prove Stop and policy/tier withdrawal; response fixtures prove
+observed usage survives observer/refresh failure. No hosted inference or visual acceptance is claimed.
