 and a delayed restore seed cannot replace any newer live main-request report.
 
+## Decision configuration through existing connections
+
+The decision role stays in Model settings → Default models, using the existing Personal writer
+and eligible classifier/chat/native connections. Its selector links directly to the chosen
+connection's original settings, or the existing Add provider entry when no connection is selected.
+The local Help identifies the two implemented consumers (on-demand judgment and automatic
+first-turn selection), cost/privacy and failure behavior; unimplemented Craft features get no switches.
+
+Dedicated sources are named TypeSafe Jev and Laya (local service), not anonymous decision-model
+products. The original Provider writer owns their URL and credentials. A System One loopback URL
+may save without a key, matching the existing backend schema; remote URLs and other protocols
+retain the key requirement. The form marks that exact optional state and recomputes it on URL
+changes. Saving a local connection does not install weights, start a server or prove availability.
+Craft's provider/settings/resolve/health/decision-point source is the comparison; Fleet does not
+copy its separate credential namespace or decision log.
+
